== Bugs ==
* If a '''Hidden Jerry''' is [[Cocooning|Cocooned]], it does not drop any loot upon being killed.

== Tips ==
* An efficient way to spawn '''Hidden ''' is mining {{Item|Cobblestone}}, {{Item|Sand}}, {{Item|Mycelium}}, or {{Item|Red Sand}} with {{Item|Mineral Armor}} or {{Item|Glossy Mineral Armor}}.
** Foraging with high amounts of {{stat|Sweep}} and Farming are also viable, but the former method results in more effective BPS than normally possible in vanilla ''Minecraft'', and therefore are better at spawning '''Hidden Jerries'''.

== Trivia ==
* When '''Hidden Jerries''' spawn, the box that initially appears displays a name tag of "Mayor Jerry's".
* If the player's '''Hidden Jerry''' dies due to fall damage, they still drop a [[Jerry Box]] as long as the player had hit it at least once.
* Like {{mt|Spooky}} [[Mobs]], the {{ench|Thunderlord}} and {{ench|Thunderbolt}} enchantments do not bypass their defense.
* Like most other [[Mobs]], '''Hidden Jerries''' can be [[Runic]], meaning they will take more hits to kill.
* [[Fishing Rods]] could at some point bypass their {{stat|def}}.
* If a '''Hidden Jerry''' is spawned inside [[Dungeons]], it is instantly killed if the player hits it.
* '''Hidden Jerries''' can open doors due to their villager entity. This then gets reverted server-side, leading to potential ghost doors.
**This can lead to decreased efficiency on the {{Zone|Garden}} if doors are used in farm designs.

